Third-party software and data in the manythreads asr image (deploy/images/asr)
==============================================================================

This file is copied into the image as /app/NOTICE. docs/deploy.md ("Speech to text") repeats the model credit.

Model
-----
NVIDIA Parakeet TDT 0.6B v3 (parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v3), a multilingual speech recognition model by NVIDIA.
  Source:   https://huggingface.co/nvidia/parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v3
  Licence:  Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC-BY-4.0), https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
The image contains an ONNX conversion of the model, int8 quantised, made by istupakov:
  https://huggingface.co/istupakov/parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v3-onnx  (same licence)
Changes: converted to ONNX and quantised to int8; no retraining. Credit goes to NVIDIA for the model.

Voice activity detection model
------------------------------
Silero VAD, a voice activity detector by the Silero team.
  Source:   https://github.com/snakers4/silero-vad
  Licence:  MIT, https://github.com/snakers4/silero-vad/blob/master/LICENSE
The image contains an ONNX copy of the model, as published by istupakov for onnx-asr: https://huggingface.co/istupakov/silero-vad-onnx  (same licence)
It cuts a clip into speech segments before the Parakeet model reads each one. No changes were made to the model.

ffmpeg (GPL)
------------
The image contains the ffmpeg program and its libraries as packaged by Debian (the `ffmpeg` package of the Debian release the python:3.12-slim base is built on).
Debian's build is licensed under the GNU General Public License (GPL version 2 or later; some parts under the LGPL).
The server only runs it as a separate program (a child process that turns an uploaded clip into raw samples); it is not linked into any other code.
The licence texts are in the image at /usr/share/doc/ffmpeg/copyright and /usr/share/common-licenses/GPL-2.
The source of the exact Debian package is available from the Debian archive (https://deb.debian.org; `apt-get source ffmpeg`).

Python packages (pinned with hashes in requirements.txt)
--------------------------------------------------------
onnx-asr (MIT) and its dependencies, with their licences as published on PyPI: onnxruntime (MIT), numpy (BSD-3-Clause), fastapi (MIT), starlette (BSD-3-Clause),
uvicorn (BSD-3-Clause), python-multipart (Apache-2.0), pydantic (MIT), huggingface-hub (Apache-2.0), protobuf (BSD-3-Clause), and the smaller packages in requirements.txt.
Each package's own licence file is installed beside it in the image (site-packages/<package>-<version>.dist-info).

Base image
----------
python:3.12-slim (Docker Official Image; Python is under the PSF licence, Debian packages under their own licences, each in /usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright).
